An AI-powered university major recommendation system for Lebanese baccalaureate students. A chatbot collects a student's grades, interests, and academic section (GS, LS, or ES),
and a machine-learning model returns the top 3 recommended majors with confidence scores.
Features


Conversational intake — a chatbot (Landbot) guides students through grades, interests, and section selection
ML-powered recommendations — top 3 majors ranked with confidence percentages, ~95% accuracy on 50,000 synthetic records across the three Lebanese baccalaureate sections (GS, LS, ES)
Real-time results — predictions delivered back through the chat flow instantly
Hardened backend — production-style API security

Frontend: React
Backend: Node.js / Express — 4 REST APIs over a normalized 10-table MySQL database
ML service: Python / Flask serving a Scikit-learn pipeline (preprocessing, feature engineering, cross-validation)
Chatbot: Landbot, connected to the backend through an ngrok tunnel during development

Backend security

MySQL accessed through a least-privilege user (no root)
Credentials and secrets in environment variables (.env, never committed)
CORS restricted to the frontend origin only
Rate limiting (10 requests per 10 minutes per client)
API-key middleware — the chatbot sends an x-api-key header; requests without a valid key get 401 Unauthorized
Sanitized errors — clients receive a generic error while full details are logged server-side



The project isnt being deployed yet so here is the steps to run the project.

What you need installed:
XAMPP (we use it for Apache and MySQL)
Node.js
Python 3
ngrok
VS Code (any editor works, but this is what we used)

First start the apache and MySQL from  xampp.
Open the frontend and the backend folders in two separate VS Code windows. In each one, open a terminal and run:
The chatbot is hosted on Landbot, so it can't reach our backend on localhost directly. We use ngrok to give the backend a temporary public URL.
open ngrok and run this command ngrok http 5001. 
Open the ml folder and type in terminal py ml_api.py.

Why isn't it deployed?
We plan to replace the Landbot chatbot with one we build ourselves using NLP, so the student can actually talk to it in normal language instead of clicking through buttons. 
We'd rather deploy once with the new chatbot than deploy twice.
